+    // Some stateful decoders (e.g. Arm Linlon MVE / mvxdec) advertise a padded
+    // coded size through G_FMT and then hand back the unpadded size from
+    // S_FMT. The padding is the driver's own bookkeeping; what has to hold is
+    // that the buffers cover the visible rectangle. Accept the driver's size in
+    // that case rather than failing to decode entirely.
+    if (!gfx::Rect(adjusted_size).Contains(visible_rect_)) {
+      // The clamp cut into the visible rectangle, which for this driver can
